# Anonymised for double-anonymous review. After acceptance: replace the authors
# with real names (and ORCIDs), add repository-code and a DOI, and complete the
# preferred citation with the proceedings details.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this replication package, please cite the paper below. The
  software and data are also citable on their own using this file.
type: software
title: >-
  Replication package for "Upgrading Is Not Migrating: Responses to the
  Model Context Protocol's First Breaking Change"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline and data for a study of MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers on
  GitHub responding to the 2026-07-28 protocol revision and the v2 SDKs:
  migration episodes mined from 32,939 repositories, a stratified labeling
  sample, coded developer text, and scripts that regenerate every number and
  figure in the paper.
authors:
  - name: Anonymous authors
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - API migration
  - breaking changes
  - software evolution
  - mining software repositories
  - technical lag
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
    Upgrading Is Not Migrating: Responses to the Model Context Protocol's
    First Breaking Change
  authors:
    - name: Anonymous authors
  collection-title: >-
    Proceedings of the IEEE International Conference on Software Analysis,
    Evolution and Reengineering (SANER)
  conference:
    name: IEEE International Conference on Software Analysis, Evolution and Reengineering (SANER 2027)
  year: 2027
